## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a real native module bridge with a practical user-facing feature that is beginner-friendly yet shows core concepts: bridging, event streams, and energy/privacy tradeoffs.

## Key Concepts

- React Native TurboModules and native bridges
- Sensor data handling and lightweight gesture detection
- Event emitters and backpressure for streams
- Battery life considerations and user privacy

## Code Example

```javascript
// skeleton: useGestureStream hook
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react'

export function useGestureStream(opts) {
  const [data, setData] = useState(null)
  useEffect(() => {
    const sub = NativeModules.MotionBridge.onGesture((e) => setData(e))
    MotionBridge.startGestureDetection(opts)
    return () => { MotionBridge.stopGestureDetection(); sub.remove() }
  }, [opts])
  return data
}
```

